That makes perfect sense! Adding a "loading circle" (a small spinner) inside the role chip visually clarifies exactly which stage the workflow is actively waiting on.
Here is the exact code replacement to add the circular progress indicator to the pending role's chip.
### VoucherAuthorization: Add Circle to Pending Role
**Find this exact line of code inside your Stepper (around the middle of the View Details Modal code):**
```javascript
                            <Chip label={getRoleDisplayName(step.role)} size="small" variant={isCurrent ? "filled" : "outlined"} color={isCurrent ? "primary" : "default"} sx={jaStyles.timelineChip} />

```
**Replace it with this:**
```javascript
                            <Chip 
                              label={getRoleDisplayName(step.role)} 
                              size="small" 
                              variant={isCurrent ? "filled" : "outlined"} 
                              color={isCurrent ? "primary" : "default"} 
                              icon={isCurrent && viewingBatchState !== "REJECTED" ? <CircularProgress size={14} color="inherit" /> : undefined}
                              sx={jaStyles.timelineChip} 
                            />

```
By adding the icon prop tied to the CircularProgress component, the active step will now automatically show a clean, small spinning circle right next to the role name. Since we set it to color="inherit", it will perfectly match the white text inside the blue primary chip!
